<item>
      <title>Pino finishes off Nottingham Forest on Glasner’s unhappy Crystal Palace return</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/11/crystal-palace-nottingham-forest-premier-league-match-report</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;It is fair to say Oliver Glasner has had more enjoyable afternoons. The Nottingham Forest head coach arrived in south London dressed like a bouncer from All Bar One in a black bomber jacket, as if he was anticipating trouble, but was instead given a rapturous reception by the home fans who used to worship him.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The generosity towards their former manager seemed to have extended to Palace’s players as Dan Ndoye was handed a goal in the third minute. Pierre Sage’s side were awful in the opening 40 minutes. Yet Forest could not find a way to beat Walter Benítez again as Liam Delap missed a golden chance to extend their lead and the Argentina goalkeeper’s heroics inspired a thrilling comeback that secured Sage’s first home victory in the Premier League since taking over from Glasner in the summer.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/11/crystal-palace-nottingham-forest-premier-league-match-report"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
